[Music]  bobsledding is a winter olympic sport  where you have your driver and you have  a brakeman which is my position the  brakeman is mainly the engine to the  sled we get it going as fast as possible  i am asia evans and i'm an olympic  bobsledder  [Music]  the track is about a mile long and full  of twists and turns and can get up to 90  miles an hour  the moment i zip up my speed suit i feel  like a complete superhero as almost like  i hear the theme music in my head i'm  ready to go  as we're going to the track picking up  speed we start to pull about five g's  which is five times the force of gravity  so it's literally what a fighter pilot  experiences  it's like someone's jumping on you  because out of nowhere you just feel all  this pressure on your lower back  it's a pretty noisy ride  my head is rattling throughout the sled  i'm trying to stay low  as soon as it's over i can inhale start  breathing again  this is one of the world's fastest  self-propelled sport  [Music]  the fastest skater will go over 50  kilometers per hour  to travel at such a high pace on the  eyes it feels that i can never get this  kind of feeling anywhere else  my name is lucas eung and i'm a short  track speed skater i have been skating  for over 20 years  but competitively only the recent 45  years  i compete with singapore but i'm right  now training in south korea  [Applause]  back in singapore a tropical country we  only have one ice rink and it's a public  ring so we only get two times of ice a  week whereas here in south korea i get  two types of ice in one day  i really like the culture of the people  here and how the whole system in the  sporting environment is  it allows me to understand the sport  better training alongside the koreans  who are the top athletes in this sport  as well  we train almost six to seven days a week  about five six hours a day pretty much  like a full-time job  it is quite a physical demanding spot  we'll do speed training we'll do  interval training we imitate the actions  and the movements on eyes and then we do  it on land so that we strengthen  the muscles needed  when i'm skating on ice it's a moment  where i feel that i'm in my own world  it feels that i have a lot of focus and  it's me and myself against the eyes and  against the speed that i'm trying to  achieve  [Music]  happy to have come so far and to have  met all the great people in the sport  and personally i feel that every time i  train and compete it makes me have this  adrenaline to want to work harder to  want to achieve greater  and not give up  [Music]  three two one see  bass jumping is already  the most dangerous sport in the world  then you're also mixing that with big  mountain skiing  you're combining full intensity sports  in an unforgiving environment the risk  factor is definitely pretty high  [Music]  hi matthias gero aka super frenchie i'm  a pro big mountain skier and  professional base jumper and i like to  put these two sports together  ski based jumping is skiing of a massive  cliff that would be too big to survive  and land safely so you use a parachute i  like to use my parachute as a tool to  ski things that i otherwise could not  ski i've been ski based swimming for 10  years and the last 10 years have been  filled with a lot of fun  the adventures i ski bass jump of the  eiger and also the meadow horn in  switzerland heavens 11 interior ride  i outran an avalanche by ski base  jumping of a 600 foot cliff  that was a pretty cool day do you see  that avalanche  fear is a it's an interesting thing your  instinct tells you okay stop right there  don't go any further this is the end of  the world right there this thing is  going to kill you this is the moment  when you have to take over and be no i'm  gonna jump off this thing and then you  come flying off this cliff  things get even faster and gnarier and  then the ground is coming straight at  you it feels like it's gonna eat you  then  the moment you land  oh man i love that time turn back look  at where you came from and then realize  that something super cool just happened  oh [ __ ] big man skiing and base jumping  is not forgiving i've definitely lost a  lot of friends over the years i've  almost died myself several times  you got to be on it you got to do the  right thing if you want to do it for a  long time that was a terrifying job it  was a close call but  hey i'm alive i'm not hurt  we did it we are looking for happiness  and some people find happiness through  balance and monotony and routine in  their life and for me that's honestly my  worst nightmare i seek happiness through  intensity  i think that intensity can bring the  best out of people  in the heart of downtown nairobi there  is a rink  that rink is home to an unnamed ice  hockey team currently  we haven't found a name for the team but  we just call it the kenya hockey team  [Music]  my name is bernard azeguere currently  the captain kenya is hockey league  i decided to play esoki simply because i  wanted to do something different  in kenya many people  we grew up playing different sports like  soccer athletics  i just want to do something that stands  out something unique  we have around 30 members in our team  we compete against ourselves  so whoever shows up we divide  the equal number of players  then we play against ourselves  [Music]  there's no money nice okay in kenya  unlike in europe where we have  leagues whereby  teams can buy players pay them well here  in kenya we're just beginning  in the next  coming years ice hockey will be a big  spot  currently many people are joining and  you're hoping to get even more as time  goes  [Music]  our future dream is for our kenyan team  to be featured in the winter olympics  i know we don't stand a chance  but  just  being there we might prove the world  wrong  once you achieve your dreams  there's a satisfaction  that comes with it  it's just a good feeling you're like  okay we've made it finally  [Music]  when i go down the slope it takes me  three seconds to get from zero to 60  miles an hour  i honestly can't explain what it feels  like even after 15 years of doing the  sport  [Music]  my name is sarah hendrickson and i'm an  olympic ski jumper  ski jumping is a sport where i go down a  two-track slope at 55 miles an hour  and when the slope ends i jump flying  about a football field in length in the  air  [Music]  when i'm getting ready to go the smell  is of the fresh air from the trees and  the snow in the area  and the feeling of cold brisk air on my  face  when i put my goggles on i know it's  time to go  [Music]  my eyesight when i'm going down the  slope is right in front of the tips of  my skis  my skis are bouncing up and down in the  track against the ice it feels like  clatter if you hear it it's like a  rumble  the flight takes three seconds but  honestly time slows down and it feels  like an eternity where i get to enjoy  flying  as i'm flying i can't hear anything it's  completely silent all around  the wind on my body feels like when you  put your hand out of a car window going  60 miles an hour moving it up and down  you can feel the lift and drag it has on  your hand  that's like ski jumping but for your  whole body  as i'm flying i'm totally alone i'm in  control of all my senses and all my  movements it's the best feeling in the  world  [Music]  you

